			<div class="content" id="post-content-2438860">
									

<p>+1</p>
<p>Started out mundane enough but got very creepy and emotional, especially in the diary. I'm a little <em>disquieted</em> right now. I'll be thinking about it for a little bit.</p>
<p>EDIT:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So I have indeed been thinking about this one on and off all day&#8230; there's so many little details that fit together, so many phrases that are caught in my head.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Manifest and attempt to consume approximately 20 kilograms of La Perruche brand individually-wrapped sugar cubes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's very sad that this poor creature's idea of a good time, like the best thing it can think to do with its powers is to manifest <em>sugar cubes.</em> Obviously because that's the only treat it was given growing up. Nice, unsettling touch.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In one recorded incident, SCP-2311 emitted a stream of liquid at an estimated pressure of</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;and one of his only known defenses is to spray people with extremely cold water&#8230; an anomalous recreation of the firehose he's known all his life. Another nice, unsettling touch.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>two unopened boxes of Rothco-brand plastic restraints.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I've yet to figure out why they're <em>unopened.</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>but the deceased appears to have undergone a botched hysterectomy.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Right, because of the mess later on where father rips out her womb and makes a weirdo cocoon out of it before waiting for it to &quot;decant.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A bassinet, a crib, and a twin-sized mattress sans bedding, all badly soiled.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No bedding, all badly soiled. Yuck.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Started searching for suitable source material. Rusty.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Nice way to say he can't get a date.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Source material arrived today. Made it official at the courthouse.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well at least he married her.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Not really all it's cracked up to be.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Nice way to show he's a virgin before this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Failing health of source material a concern.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Urgh. Didn't catch this on my first readthrough. So he's probably got her chained up in the basement and not taking good care of her, and raping her.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The womb is simply that primordial void of so many creation myths. A vacuum paradoxically containing all necessities for creation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A really good line&#8230; an fascinating idea that breaks out of creep for a second, then dives right back in.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Blurred gender as much as I could without risking critical defect; masculine + feminine, sun + moon, yin + yang, all that good shit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Great bits in here which explain the deformities.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Alterations continue. Parted the waters and drove the heart from the center.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I still don't know what this means, but I don't think it's good. Is this the hysterectomy?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Vessel spent and disposed of. Think I earned a fucking drink.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Just&#8230; just awful. He killed her in a horrible, inhumane way without a second thought and all he can think is, &quot;All in a day's work.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>nitrohydrochloric acid</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I only just realized why he keeps bringing this up. This is man's name for the chemical, and because he can't &quot;unlearn&quot; this name, he can't get it to work magically.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Well done!</p>

							</div>

								
