			<div class="content" id="post-content-2438977">
									

<p>For what it's worth, I know &quot;spooky magic kid&quot; is a cliche and that &quot;poor widdle reality bender&quot; is a trope so popular on this site that it's rapidly approaching cliche. I was close to abandoning this project early on for those reasons, but people seemed to like the manuscript enough that I was encouraged to go for it. But I'll admit this piece is leaning very hard on the manuscript, which is why I spent a lot of time and effort on that section in particular. I wrote most of the prop on the subway and probably creeped some commuters out with my arts and crafts time, heh.</p>
<p>I'm of the opinion that solid execution can overcome the fact that an idea has been done before. I'm glad all the effort I put into &quot;daddy's&quot; manuscript at least saved me from your down vote. I knew going in this wouldn't be everyone's cup of tea, so I'm going to round this up to a win.</p>

